.Dd Jul 23, 2026
.Dt XTC_PROB 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_bloom_init ,
.Nm xtc_bloom_add ,
.Nm xtc_bloom_maybe_contains ,
.Nm xtc_bloom_fini ,
.Nm xtc_hll_init ,
.Nm xtc_hll_add ,
.Nm xtc_hll_count ,
.Nm xtc_hll_merge ,
.Nm xtc_hll_fini
.Nd Bloom filter and HyperLogLog cardinality estimator
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc.h
.In xtc_prob.h
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_bloom_init "xtc_bloom_t **out" "size_t n_expected" "double fp_rate"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_bloom_add "xtc_bloom_t *b" "const void *key" "size_t len"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_bloom_maybe_contains "const xtc_bloom_t *b" "const void *key" "size_t len"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_bloom_fini "xtc_bloom_t *b"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_hll_init "xtc_hll_t **out" "int precision"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_hll_add "xtc_hll_t *h" "const void *key" "size_t len"
.Ft uint64_t
.Fn xtc_hll_count "const xtc_hll_t *h"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_hll_merge "xtc_hll_t *dst" "const xtc_hll_t *src"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_hll_fini "xtc_hll_t *h"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm xtc_prob
provides two probabilistic sketches that trade a small, bounded,
tunable error for memory that stays flat no matter how many distinct
keys pass through: a Bloom filter for approximate set membership and a
HyperLogLog for approximate distinct-count estimation.
Keys are opaque byte spans
.Pq Fa key , Fa len ,
hashed internally, so any key type works with no caller-supplied hash
or comparator; nothing is copied or retained, so a key buffer may be
freed the moment the call returns.
.Pp
Both structures are
.Em single-threaded
in this version: unlike
.Xr xtc_chash 3
and
.Xr xtc_cskip 3
there is no internal locking and no RCU.  Concurrent
.Fn xtc_bloom_add
or
.Fn xtc_hll_add
on one instance is a data race.  Serialize externally, or give each
thread its own instance and
.Pq for HLL
combine them with
.Fn xtc_hll_merge ,
which is an exact register-wise maximum.
.Ss Bloom filter
A bit array of
.Va m
bits probed by
.Va k
hash functions.
.Fn xtc_bloom_init
derives the optimal
.Va m
and
.Va k
from the expected element count
.Fa n_expected
and the target false-positive rate
.Fa fp_rate
.Pq strictly between 0 and 1 :
.Va m No = ceil(-n*ln(p) / (ln2)^2)
and
.Va k No = round((m/n)*ln2) .
.Fn xtc_bloom_add
sets the
.Va k
bits for a key
.Pq adding the same key twice is idempotent .
.Fn xtc_bloom_maybe_contains
returns 1 if the key MAY be present and 0 if it is DEFINITELY absent:
there are NO false negatives
.Pq every added key returns 1 ,
and a 1 result carries the configured false-positive probability once
the filter holds about
.Fa n_expected
elements.  The filter does not resize; loading it well past
.Fa n_expected
raises the false-positive rate, so size it for the true expected load.
.Fn xtc_bloom_fini
frees it.
.Ss HyperLogLog
.Fn xtc_hll_init
allocates 2^ Ns Fa precision
registers;
.Fa precision
must be in the range 4 to 18
.Pq 16 to 262144 registers .
Each register holds the maximum leading-zero run seen for the hashes
that fall in its bucket.
.Fn xtc_hll_add
folds a key in.
.Fn xtc_hll_count
returns the estimated number of DISTINCT keys added, using the
bias-corrected harmonic-mean estimator with the standard small-range
.Pq linear-counting
and large-range corrections; the relative standard error is about
1.04/sqrt(2^ Ns Fa precision Ns ) -- roughly 1.6% at precision 12 and
well under 1% at precision 16 -- in a few kilobytes regardless of the
true cardinality.
.Fn xtc_hll_merge
takes the register-wise max of
.Fa src
into
.Fa dst ,
so
.Fa dst
afterward estimates the cardinality of the UNION of the two key sets
with no error added by the merge; both sketches must have the same
precision.
.Fn xtc_hll_fini
frees it.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xtc_bloom_init ,
.Fn xtc_hll_init ,
and
.Fn xtc_hll_merge
return
.Dv XTC_OK
on success,
.Dv XTC_E_INVAL
for a NULL out-pointer, an
.Fa fp_rate
not in the open interval
.Pq 0,1 ,
an out-of-range
.Fa precision ,
or mismatched precisions at merge, and
.Dv XTC_E_NOMEM
on allocation failure.
.Fn xtc_bloom_maybe_contains
returns 1 (maybe present) or 0 (definitely absent; also 0 for a NULL
filter).
.Fn xtc_hll_count
returns the estimated distinct-key count
.Pq 0 for a NULL sketch .
.Fn xtc_bloom_add ,
.Fn xtc_hll_add ,
.Fn xtc_bloom_fini ,
and
.Fn xtc_hll_fini
have no return value and treat a NULL instance as a no-op.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xtc_bloom_t *b;
xtc_bloom_init(&b, 100000, 0.01);      /* 1% false positives */
xtc_bloom_add(b, "answer", 6);
if (xtc_bloom_maybe_contains(b, "answer", 6))
	printf("maybe present\en");     /* always true for an added key */
if (!xtc_bloom_maybe_contains(b, "nope", 4))
	printf("definitely absent\en"); /* usually true */
xtc_bloom_fini(b);

xtc_hll_t *h;
xtc_hll_init(&h, 14);                    /* 2^14 registers */
for (int i = 0; i < 1000000; i++)
	xtc_hll_add(h, &i, sizeof i);
printf("~%llu distinct\en",
    (unsigned long long)xtc_hll_count(h));
xtc_hll_fini(h);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_chash 3 ,
.Xr xtc_cskip 3 ,
.Xr xtc 7
.Sh HISTORY
